Section: libs
Priority: optional
Description: Mesa 26.3.0-devel (turnip/freedreno) for the OnePlus Pad 3 (erhai)
 Out-of-tree Mesa build for the Adreno 830 (gen8_0_1) in the OnePlus Pad 3,
 installed under /opt/mesa so it never shadows the system Mesa.
 .
 Ubuntu's Mesa is too old for gen8: its freedreno gallium driver refuses the
 chip ("failed to create dri2 screen") and its turnip does not recognise the
 chip id, so GL falls back to llvmpipe and every hardware-accelerated Vulkan
 client fails. This build supports the part both ways -- native freedreno
 gallium (GL_RENDERER=FD830) and Vulkan 1.4 turnip, with zink on top of it as
 the alternative GL path.
 .
 Nothing is activated by installing this package. The desktop session opts in
 through environment variables (VK_DRIVER_FILES, LD_LIBRARY_PATH,
 __EGL_VENDOR_LIBRARY_FILENAMES); a ready-made drop-in is shipped at
 /usr/share/oneplus-erhai-mesa/10-desktop.conf.gpu, which is what
 erhai-desktop-gl.service installs into the user's environment.d when the
 kernel has the GPU enabled.

