Section: utils
Priority: optional
Description: Hexagon NPU / compute-DSP (CDSP) stack for the OnePlus Pad 3 (erhai)
 Brings the Hexagon COMPUTE DSP (CDSP) up to userspace. The Hexagon NPU
 (HTP, Hexagon Tensor Processor) is not a standalone device: it hangs off the
 CDSP and is driven by DSP-side firmware and libraries (libhcp_rpc_skel.so,
 libhcpfrc.so, ubwcdma_dynlib.so, libQnnHtpV79Skel.so) that the AP loads over
 FastRPC. This package provides everything on the AP side of that path:
  - the complete CDSP FastRPC remotefs tree served to the DSP
    (/var/lib/hexagonfs-cdsp/dsp/cdsp): fastrpc_shell_3 +
    fastrpc_shell_unsigned_3 (the user-PD shells), the Hexagon CoProcessor
    (HTP) runtime libs from the device's own dsp partition, the vendor QNN
    HTP v79 skel (libQnnHtpV79Skel.so) and the C++ runtime the skels link
    against -- all taken from OxygenOS 16.0.9.400;
  - hexagonrpcd-cdsp.service: a second hexagonrpcd instance (the upstream
    open-source FastRPC daemon) attaching to /dev/fastrpc-cdsp in "rootpd"
    mode, the Linux equivalent of Android's `cdsprpcd rootpd cdsp`;
  - erhai-npu-status.sh: one-shot health report of the whole chain
    (kernel DT/firmware, remoteproc, FastRPC nodes, daemon, dmesg evidence).
 .
 Kernel side (oneplus-erhai-linux >= +b63 + oneplus-erhai-firmware >= 1.2):
 &remoteproc_cdsp enabled with the OxygenOS cdsp.mdt/cdsp_dtb.mdt split image
 and the OEM-identical carveouts (0x9d200000+0x1900000, 0x9eb00000+0x80000).
 .
 NOTE: the QNN *host* runtime (libQnnHtp.so / libQnnHtpV79Stub.so) is not
 shippable -- Qualcomm only distributes it for Android (bionic) and through
 the account-gated QNN/Hexagon SDK. The skel and the HTP runtime are present
 here, so the NPU itself is bring-up complete; driving a graph additionally
 needs a glibc QNN host runtime.

